---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const site = 'https://www.ewohub.com';
const slug = 'webcam-earnings-by-platform';
---

<Base
  title="Webcam Earnings by Platform — Chaturbate vs Stripchat vs BongaCams vs LiveJasmin"
  description="A real breakdown of how much webcam models earn on Chaturbate, Stripchat, BongaCams, and LiveJasmin — payout rates, token values, and what actually drives the difference."
  lang="en"
  hreflang={[
    { lang: 'en', url: `${site}/webcam-earnings-by-platform` },
    { lang: 'de', url: `${site}/de/webcam-earnings-by-platform` },
    { lang: 'es', url: `${site}/es/webcam-earnings-by-platform` },
    { lang: 'ro', url: `${site}/ro/webcam-earnings-by-platform` },
    { lang: 'uk', url: `${site}/uk/webcam-earnings-by-platform` },
    { lang: 'ru', url: `${site}/ru/webcam-earnings-by-platform` },
  ]}
>

<!-- HERO -->
<div class="art-hero">
  <div class="art-orb art-orb--1"></div>
  <div class="art-orb art-orb--2"></div>
  <div class="art-grid"></div>
  <div class="art-hero__inner container">
    <div class="art-meta">
      <span class="art-tag">Guide</span>
      <span class="art-tag">Platform Comparison</span>
      <span class="art-tag art-tag--green">
        <span class="dot-green"></span>
        Real payout data
      </span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="art-title">Webcam Earnings<br><span class="art-grad">by Platform</span></h1>
    <p class="art-lead">Every platform advertises a different payout percentage, and every percentage tells only part of the story. This is a straight comparison of how Chaturbate, Stripchat, BongaCams, and LiveJasmin actually pay — token values, payout tiers, and what really determines which one earns you more.</p>
    <div class="art-stats-row">
      <div class="art-stat-item">
        <span class="art-stat-num">4</span>
        <span class="art-stat-lab">Platforms compared</span>
      </div>
      <div class="art-stat-div"></div>
      <div class="art-stat-item">
        <span class="art-stat-num">$0.05</span>
        <span class="art-stat-lab">Typical token value</span>
      </div>
      <div class="art-stat-div"></div>
      <div class="art-stat-item">
        <span class="art-stat-num">30–80%</span>
        <span class="art-stat-lab">Payout range</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- BODY -->
<div class="art-body container">
  <div class="art-layout">

    <!-- TOC -->
    <aside class="art-toc">
      <p class="art-toc__title">Contents</p>
      <ol class="art-toc__list">
        <li><a href="#how-payouts-work">How payouts work</a></li>
        <li><a href="#chaturbate">Chaturbate</a></li>
        <li><a href="#stripchat">Stripchat</a></li>
        <li><a href="#bongacams">BongaCams</a></li>
        <li><a href="#livejasmin">LiveJasmin</a></li>
        <li><a href="#which-pays-most">Which pays most?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#multi-platform">Multi-platform</a></li>
      </ol>
      <a href="#cta" class="art-toc__cta">Get a free audit →</a>
    </aside>

    <!-- Main -->
    <main class="art-main">

      <p class="art-intro">See also: <a href="/webcam-model-income-guide">our full income guide →</a> for what actually drives earnings beyond the platform you pick.</p>

      <!-- SECTION 1 -->
      <div class="reason-card" id="how-payouts-work">
        <div class="reason-num">01</div>
        <div class="reason-content">
          <h2>How Payout Percentages Actually Work</h2>
          <p>Every major cam platform runs on a token or credit system. Viewers buy tokens for real money, then spend them in your room via tips, goals, and private shows. The platform sets both the price viewers pay per token and the rate it pays you per token — the gap between those two numbers is the platform's cut.</p>

          <div class="highlight-box">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M13 2L3 14h9l-1 8 10-12h-9l1-8z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            <p>Two platforms can advertise the same <strong>"60% payout"</strong> and still leave you with very different real earnings, because token prices, tier requirements, and payout thresholds differ. The percentage alone doesn't tell you what you'll actually take home.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- CHATURBATE -->
      <div class="reason-card" id="chaturbate">
        <div class="reason-num">02</div>
        <div class="reason-content">
          <h2>Chaturbate</h2>
          <p>Chaturbate pays a flat <strong>$0.05 per token</strong> for standard broadcasters — this doesn't scale up with how much you earn, unlike most competitors. Models who qualify for Fan Club status can earn <strong>$0.06–$0.08 per token</strong>, and high-volume broadcasters can negotiate custom rates directly with the platform. Viewers typically pay $0.08–$0.11 per token depending on the package they buy, which puts Chaturbate's effective cut at roughly <strong>40–50%</strong>.</p>

          <div class="pull-quote">
            <svg class="pull-quote__icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M3 21c3 0 7-1 7-8V5c0-1.25-.756-2.017-2-2H4c-1.25 0-2 .75-2 1.972V11c0 1.25.75 2 2 2 1 0 1 0 1 1v1c0 1-1 2-2 2s-1 .008-1 1.031V20c0 1 0 1 1 1zm12 0c3 0 7-1 7-8V5c0-1.25-.757-2.017-2-2h-4c-1.25 0-2 .75-2 1.972V11c0 1.25.75 2 2 2h.75c0 2.25.25 4-2.75 4v3c0 1 0 1 1 1z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            Chaturbate's lower rate is often offset by the largest concurrent viewer base of any cam platform — higher traffic volume frequently outearns a higher percentage on a smaller platform.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- STRIPCHAT -->
      <div class="reason-card" id="stripchat">
        <div class="reason-num">03</div>
        <div class="reason-content">
          <h2>Stripchat</h2>
          <p>Stripchat pays <strong>50–60%</strong> of token value, with the exact rate depending on your model status and where your traffic comes from. Token value is also around $0.05, with the platform keeping roughly 37–52% depending on which token package the viewer purchased. New models typically start around 50% and can work up toward 60% as their account status improves.</p>

          <div class="two-col-box">
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--bad">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">New models</p>
              <p>~50% payout rate — standard starting rate for new accounts</p>
            </div>
            <div class="two-col-box__item two-col-box__item--good">
              <p class="two-col-box__label">Established models</p>
              <p>Up to 60% as account status and traffic source improve</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- BONGACAMS -->
      <div class="reason-card" id="bongacams">
        <div class="reason-num">04</div>
        <div class="reason-content">
          <h2>BongaCams</h2>
          <p>BongaCams uses a tiered system that's wider than most — reported rates range from <strong>25% up to 60–65%</strong> depending on your earnings level, with some top-tier claims reaching higher still. Token value is fixed at $0.05. Payouts run on a bi-weekly schedule with a $50 minimum threshold.</p>

          <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--warning">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 001.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 001.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 00-3.42 0z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            <p>The wide tier range means two BongaCams models can have <strong>very different effective payout rates</strong> depending purely on how much volume they've built up — the headline percentage only applies to top performers.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- LIVEJASMIN -->
      <div class="reason-card" id="livejasmin">
        <div class="reason-num">05</div>
        <div class="reason-content">
          <h2>LiveJasmin</h2>
          <p>LiveJasmin runs the steepest tiered structure of the four: new models start at the bottom tier around <strong>30%</strong>, standard active models reach up to <strong>60%</strong>, and the platform's highest tier (Level 9, reserved for models earning $30,000+ every two months) can pay up to <strong>80%</strong>.</p>
          <p>Tiers are reassessed each pay period based on earnings in that window, so your rate can move both up and down. This structure rewards high, consistent volume more aggressively than the other three platforms.</p>

          <div class="checklist">
            <p class="checklist__title">LiveJasmin tier reality check:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M15 9l-6 6M9 9l6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
                New models start at ~30% — the lowest of any major platform
              </li>
              <li>
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M15 9l-6 6M9 9l6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
                Tiers reset every pay period — a bad month drops your rate
              </li>
              <li class="ok">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                High-volume models can reach 80% — the best rate in the industry
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- WHICH PAYS MOST -->
      <div class="reason-card" id="which-pays-most">
        <div class="reason-num">06</div>
        <div class="reason-content">
          <h2>So Which Platform Actually Pays the Most?</h2>
          <p>There's no single answer, and any guide that gives you one flat ranking is oversimplifying. What actually determines your real income is the combination of:</p>

          <div class="fix-box">
            <div class="fix-box__header">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              The 4 real factors
            </div>
            <p><strong>Traffic volume</strong> — Chaturbate's lower headline rate is often offset by having far more concurrent viewers than smaller platforms.<br><br>
            <strong>Tier difficulty</strong> — LiveJasmin and BongaCams's top rates require sustained high earnings to unlock; if you can't consistently hit the tier, the headline percentage is irrelevant.<br><br>
            <strong>Audience fit</strong> — each platform skews toward a different viewer base; the platform whose audience matches your content will outearn a "higher-paying" platform with the wrong audience.<br><br>
            <strong>Studio vs. independent</strong> — if you stream through a studio, the studio's cut (commonly 30–70%) applies on top of the platform's own rate.</p>
          </div>

          <p>In practice, the models earning the most aren't necessarily on the platform with the best advertised percentage — they're on the platform where their traffic and audience actually convert. See: <a href="/platforms-we-work-with">how we match models to platforms →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- MULTI-PLATFORM -->
      <div class="reason-card" id="multi-platform">
        <div class="reason-num">07</div>
        <div class="reason-content">
          <h2>Multi-Platform Strategy</h2>
          <p>Established models increasingly stream across more than one platform — either simultaneously (multistreaming) or on a rotating schedule — to capture a higher blended payout without depending on a single platform's traffic or tier rules.</p>

          <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--warning">
            <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 001.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 001.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 00-3.42 0z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            <p>This isn't the right move for <strong>new models</strong> still building a first audience. Split attention before you've established momentum anywhere usually costs more than the extra platform earns.</p>
          </div>

          <p>It becomes worthwhile once you have a reliable base on at least one platform. Read more: <a href="/webcam-model-income-guide">the full income guide →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ -->
      <section class="faq-section">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Is a higher payout percentage always better?
            <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p>No. A higher percentage on a platform with less traffic, a harder-to-reach tier, or a mismatched audience frequently earns less in absolute terms than a lower percentage on a platform where your content actually finds viewers. Percentage is one input, not the answer.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Do these payout rates apply to studio models the same way?
            <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p>The platform pays out at the same rates regardless of whether you're independent or with a studio — but studio models receive their share after the studio takes its own cut (commonly 30–70% of what the studio collects from the platform), so the studio's terms matter as much as the platform's payout rate.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>
            Should I stream on the platform with the highest payout tier?
            <svg class="faq-chevron" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          </summary>
          <p>Only if you can realistically sustain the volume that tier requires, and only if that platform's audience fits your content. Chasing a high tier on a platform where you can't generate consistent traffic usually earns less than a moderate, reliable rate on a platform where you actually convert.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA -->
      <div class="art-cta" id="cta">
        <div class="art-cta__orb"></div>
        <div class="art-cta__inner">
          <div class="art-cta__badge">The real equation</div>
          <h2>The Platform Matters Less Than the Traffic Behind It</h2>
          <p>Every payout tier on every platform assumes you already have viewers to convert. Our promotion service is built to solve the traffic side of the equation, whichever platform you're on.</p>
          <div class="art-cta__actions">
            <a href="https://t.me/+tBjfmjh9vHo1YzQy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="art-cta__btn art-cta__btn--primary">
              <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M21 2L2 9l7 4 2 7 10-18z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              Get a free promotion audit
            </a>
            <a href="/platforms-we-work-with" class="art-cta__btn art-cta__btn--ghost">Platforms we work with →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- RELATED -->
      <section class="related-section">
        <h2>Related Articles</h2>
        <div class="related-grid">
          <a href="/webcam-model-income-guide" class="related-card">
            <div class="related-card__icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="23" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 000 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 010 7H6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p>Webcam Model Income Guide</p>
            <span>Read →</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/platforms-we-work-with" class="related-card">
            <div class="related-card__icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M19.07 4.93a10 10 0 010 14.14M4.93 4.93a10 10 0 000 14.14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p>Platforms We Work With</p>
            <span>Read →</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/how-cam-algorithm-ranks-rooms" class="related-card">
            <div class="related-card__icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p>How the Cam Algorithm Ranks Rooms</p>
            <span>Read →</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/model-promotion" class="related-card">
            <div class="related-card__icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M21 2L2 9l7 4 2 7 10-18z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p>Model Promotion Services</p>
            <span>Read →</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/best-streaming-times-by-region" class="related-card">
            <div class="related-card__icon">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M12 6v6l4 2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            </div>
            <p>Best Streaming Times by Region</p>
            <span>Read →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </main>
  </div>
</div>

</Base>
